WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:08.999
Tomorrow morning,

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.417
everyone will wake up fully recharged...

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:15.041
except Lilypad.

00:00:15.042 --> 00:00:18.500
And then we'll make Lily
tell us... Where's Jessie?

00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:24.874
[Blaze snoring]

00:00:24.875 --> 00:00:26.708
Oh, finally.

00:00:31.875 --> 00:00:32.957
Psst. Hey.

00:00:32.958 --> 00:00:34.416
[Smarty Pants] It's okay. Just ignore her.

00:00:34.417 --> 00:00:35.999
- [Atlas] Shh, shh.
- [Snappy] Quiet!

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.500
[Smarty Pants] Nobody's home.

00:00:38.125 --> 00:00:40.499
- I can hear you.
- [Snappy] Smarty!

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.541
- What? I used a faraway voice.
- [Atlas] Come on, man!

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:44.457
- Look. Camera--
- It's Snappy.

00:00:44.458 --> 00:00:45.582
Right, Snappy.

00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:47.374
You said there was a way you could help us

00:00:47.375 --> 00:00:48.957
get to Bonnie, right? So, what is it?

00:00:48.958 --> 00:00:51.082
[Smarty Pants]
She did say that, didn't she?

00:00:51.083 --> 00:00:52.916
That sounds, I don't know...

00:00:52.917 --> 00:00:55.124
- [Snappy] Useful?
- That's it, yeah.

00:00:55.125 --> 00:00:57.457
Too bad we're useless!

00:00:57.458 --> 00:00:59.667
- [Snappy] Right!
- [Atlas] Yeah! Remember?

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.124
- [blusters]
- [sighs]

00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:04.999
I'm sorry I called you useless.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.833
You three are definitely of use...

00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:11.708
somehow.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.374
- [Snappy] Worst apology ever.
- [Atlas] Just awful.

00:01:14.375 --> 00:01:16.541
[Smarty Pants] Now I want
an apology for that apology.

00:01:16.542 --> 00:01:18.166
[sighs]

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:21.583
Please. I know I messed up.

00:01:22.083 --> 00:01:25.166
I was wrong about your kid, Blaze.

00:01:25.167 --> 00:01:29.499
She's creative and silly

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:32.250
in a way other kids don't really get.

00:01:32.875 --> 00:01:34.208
[stammers] Am I right?

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:44.625
Go on.

00:01:45.208 --> 00:01:47.582
Well, our kid's like that too.

00:01:47.583 --> 00:01:50.041
And I think they'd really like each other.

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:52.332
So, fine, if you don't want to help me,

00:01:52.333 --> 00:01:54.292
let's just help our kids.

00:01:55.708 --> 00:01:57.249
All right, twist my handle.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.749
Yeah! We're making friends.

00:01:58.750 --> 00:02:00.124
- F-R-E-N-D.
- With an "I."

00:02:00.125 --> 00:02:01.207
[Snappy] F-R-I-N-D.

00:02:01.208 --> 00:02:03.249
Great! So, how do we connect them?

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:06.374
You said your kid's device was
on The Pond like me, right?

00:02:06.375 --> 00:02:10.416
Right! So Smarty, Atlas and I
are all compatible, see?

00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:12.207
And I could take a picture of you.

00:02:12.208 --> 00:02:14.375
- Okay, act like a toy.
- O-Okay.

00:02:16.333 --> 00:02:18.291
Uh, not very photogenic, are they?

00:02:18.292 --> 00:02:20.082
- And Atlas can add text to it.
- Mm-hmm.

00:02:20.083 --> 00:02:21.499
FOUND YOUR TOYS!

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.624
- Then we post it on The Pond.
- [Atlas] Yep.

00:02:23.625 --> 00:02:24.707
Where Bonnie is!

00:02:24.708 --> 00:02:26.124
[all] Ta-da!

00:02:26.125 --> 00:02:27.957
- Great! So, you sent it?
- [♪ gentle music playing]

00:02:27.958 --> 00:02:29.416
No. Still going.

00:02:29.417 --> 00:02:31.000
[sighs]

00:02:33.083 --> 00:02:34.207
How about now?

00:02:34.208 --> 00:02:36.707
[exclaims] Still going.

00:02:36.708 --> 00:02:38.749
Still going? How is that possible?

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.916
Look at my eyes! The little
toilet roll's still spinning.

00:02:40.917 --> 00:02:42.582
I'm only as fast as my operating system.

00:02:42.583 --> 00:02:44.667
So just slow your roll, all right?

00:02:45.917 --> 00:02:47.499
- [chimes]
- There. It's sent.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.082
Finally. Now what?

00:02:50.083 --> 00:02:51.207
Now, we wait.

00:02:51.208 --> 00:02:52.499
Yeah, everyone's still asleep.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:54.582
We gotta wait for Bonnie
to wake up and see the post.

00:02:54.583 --> 00:02:57.083
[groans, sighs]

00:02:59.208 --> 00:03:01.874
Hey, I know! We could play a game.

00:03:01.875 --> 00:03:02.791
- Yes!
- Yeah!

00:03:02.792 --> 00:03:03.707
- A game?
- Yeah!

00:03:03.708 --> 00:03:05.082
It was Blaze's favorite.

00:03:05.083 --> 00:03:06.749
It's called "Pick the Poop."

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:07.957
You try and hit the button

00:03:07.958 --> 00:03:09.916
when the poop shows up over it.

00:03:09.917 --> 00:03:11.208
Hey, Smarty.

00:03:12.083 --> 00:03:15.916
I will never play that game.

00:03:15.917 --> 00:03:19.167
[chuckles] They all say that.

00:03:20.375 --> 00:03:22.374
[insects chirping]

00:03:22.375 --> 00:03:23.749
[child laughing]

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:24.666
[sibling] Come on!

00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:26.624
- It's my turn.
- [mom] Okay, you two.

00:03:26.625 --> 00:03:28.874
Time to stop playing with your new toy.

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:30.791
- It's bedtime.
- [children groan]

00:03:30.792 --> 00:03:32.874
- Already?
- Do we have to?

00:03:32.875 --> 00:03:34.791
- [mom] Yeah, come on.
- [children groan]

00:03:34.792 --> 00:03:36.875
[♪ tense music playing]

00:04:08.458 --> 00:04:09.666
[laptop beeps]

00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:10.750
Huh?

00:04:20.125 --> 00:04:25.291
[mom] "And they had splendid
games together, in whispers,

00:04:25.292 --> 00:04:28.124
when Nana had gone away to her supper

00:04:28.125 --> 00:04:29.999
and left the night-light burning

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.667
on the mantelpiece.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:35.374
And when the boy dropped off to sleep,

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:39.707
the rabbit would snuggle down close under

00:04:39.708 --> 00:04:41.332
- his little, warm chin..."
- [beeping]

00:04:41.333 --> 00:04:42.416
Sir.

00:04:42.417 --> 00:04:45.874
"...and dream with the boy's hands

00:04:45.875 --> 00:04:49.542
clasped close round him all night."

00:04:55.958 --> 00:04:57.208
Hmm.

00:04:58.417 --> 00:05:00.624
- [gasp] Star Command.
- Star Command.

00:05:00.625 --> 00:05:02.083
- Star Command.
- Star Command.

00:05:08.583 --> 00:05:10.750
[all] Star Command.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:14.833
- [birds chirping]
- [groans]

00:05:15.958 --> 00:05:19.000
[yawns, sighs]

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:21.416
What? No, no, no!

00:05:21.417 --> 00:05:22.999
Dad! Dad!

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.124
What? What is it?

00:05:24.125 --> 00:05:26.624
Lily's not working!
I'm missing Turtle Tag!

00:05:26.625 --> 00:05:28.957
Kara, Chelsea and Heidi
play it every morning.

00:05:28.958 --> 00:05:31.166
- I can't miss it, Dad!
- It's okay.

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:32.249
I plugged it back in.

00:05:32.250 --> 00:05:33.624
We just need to wait for it to charge.

00:05:33.625 --> 00:05:35.874
But it's not okay!
I'm gonna miss the game!

00:05:35.875 --> 00:05:37.957
Sweetie, there's nothing
we can do for now.

00:05:37.958 --> 00:05:39.874
- [Bonnie groans]
- [door closes]

00:05:39.875 --> 00:05:42.499
Aha! Success, huh? Look at that.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:43.582
That's phase one.

00:05:43.583 --> 00:05:45.375
- And now, phase two.
- Phase two.

00:05:45.875 --> 00:05:47.541
Well, I thought I was gonna
initiate phase two.

00:05:47.542 --> 00:05:49.916
I initiate phase two.
We thumb wrestled over this.

00:05:49.917 --> 00:05:51.042
All right, fine.

00:05:51.583 --> 00:05:53.707
And then we'll have a little talk

00:05:53.708 --> 00:05:55.667
with our froggy friend.

00:05:56.375 --> 00:05:59.291
- [toy beeping]
- [Blaze snoring]

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:01.166
[grunting]

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:03.957
- One, two, one, two, two...
- I hate this game.

00:06:03.958 --> 00:06:05.666
- ...one, two, one...
- Please make it stop.

00:06:05.667 --> 00:06:07.124
MIGHTY WIPER!

00:06:07.125 --> 00:06:08.957
- Mighty Wiper!
- [Atlas shushes]

00:06:08.958 --> 00:06:11.041
- Again, again, again!
- I think you need a break.

00:06:11.042 --> 00:06:12.124
I can't feel my buttons.

00:06:12.125 --> 00:06:15.416
- Just one more time! Come on!
- That's enough play for now.

00:06:15.417 --> 00:06:16.499
Play? [scoffs]

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.541
That's just a game. That's not playing.

00:06:18.542 --> 00:06:19.541
What's the difference?

00:06:19.542 --> 00:06:21.083
You know, real play.

00:06:22.792 --> 00:06:24.291
You're kidding, right?

00:06:24.292 --> 00:06:26.208
You've never seen Blaze play with a toy?

00:06:27.583 --> 00:06:28.874
How long were you guys with her?

00:06:28.875 --> 00:06:29.957
- Three months.
- Ten months.

00:06:29.958 --> 00:06:31.041
- Six months.
- Months?

00:06:31.042 --> 00:06:31.999
What? Too long?

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.166
Too short! [groans]
Guys, you missed all the fun!

00:06:35.167 --> 00:06:36.124
Hey, we're fun.

00:06:36.125 --> 00:06:38.958
I mean fun, fun. Make-believe fun.

